<title>USA: TABLE-Primary Bank Q2 shr loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Primary Bank Q2 shr loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>PETERBOROUGH, N.H. 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr loss		   $0.07   profit	 $0.37</p>
<p> Net loss		     140   profit	   786</p>
<p> Net int. income	  3,872		    3,214</p>
<p> Nonint. income	     780			707</p>
<p> Loan loss prov	     600			242</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   2,089		    2,106</p>
<p>	  6  MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr profit		 $0.32   profit	 $0.74</p>
<p> Net profit		   739   profit	 1,573</p>
<p> Net int. incom	   7,531		    6,476</p>
<p> Nonint. income	   1,431		    1,236</p>
<p> Loan loss prov	     750			296</p>
<p> Total assets	   431,683		  408,086</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   2,277		    2,105</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers. Return in equity is in percent.)</p>
<p>NOTE: The loss in Q2 1997 reflects, in part, the recording of a first time charge to compensation expense of $798,000 to reflect performance-based stock options which vest if the market price of the bank's shares reaches certain stated levels.</p>
<p>During the quarter, common stock price levels increased sufficiently for vesting of 67,675 performance based options.</p>
<p>Without that charge, the quarter would have been profitable.</p>
</text>
